1
00:00:00,530 --> 00:00:06,520
Just before eleven at night, your manager texts the night crew. Storm's early. Lock up behind the last customer.

2
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:11,920
Three of you are working tonight. You. Dana, who has the keys. And Marcus, who drives the forklift.

3
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:16,450
The forecast says a foot and a half of snow by morning. The roads close at midnight.

4
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:22,910
Nobody's worried. The store has enough water to fill a swimming pool. Worst case, you sleep in the bedding aisle.

5
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:26,940
At two in the morning, you're restocking aisle fourteen when the lights flicker.

6
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:28,770
Then the freezers go quiet.

7
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:32,100
The generator kicks in. Only half the lights come back.

8
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:38,640
By four, the wind has piled snow against the front doors. Dana pushes. They open two inches and stop.

9
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:45,640
Marcus checks the loading dock. The bay camera shows nothing but white. Snow, packed against the lens, eight feet up.

10
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:51,080
Your phone has one bar. The county alert says plows are suspended. Stay where you are.

11
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:58,880
Dana does the math out loud. The generator has fuel for three days. And every freezer in the store is already starting to drip.

12
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:01,700
Then she pulls up the cameras to check the other doors.

13
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,150
Camera six. Aisle twenty-two. Pet food.

14
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:07,900
Someone is sitting on the floor, eating out of a bag.

15
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:12,200
Dana locked the doors at eleven. Nobody came in after that.

16
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,350
Which means they were already inside.
